      <workList xml:id="workDesc_d3c5d3ef">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e240237">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_e362f8e4">B5:Coll.001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_171N200DE" xml:lang="de">Arien mit unterschiedlichen Teutschen und Dänischen Texten</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_42ff1d40">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_8f88399b">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_171N200EC">
               <p xml:id="idm82">The present collection contains 41 arias (‘Lieder’ or ‘Oden’) for voice and figured bass by various composers and authors. Music to one of the arias is most likely by Scheibe (SchW B5:100), while the texts to the remaining eight ones are by Scheibe (indicated by ‘J.A.S.’ placed below the title of the aria). Among other composers are <persName xml:id="idm83" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Georg Philipp Telemann</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm84" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">George Frederic Handel</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm85" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Foltmar</persName> who most likely is also the copyist. The transcript was made on paper which may be dated to around 1770–71.</p>
            </history>
