               <watermark xml:id="watermark_a07aecd9">a visible emblem consisting of two letters ('S' and 'M') crowned and with an 'I D' (Johann Drewsen; cf. Heawood:3217, and Lassen:IV.14a), Danish produced paper dated to 1770–71.</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_138d57e0">In 4<rend xml:id="idm41" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format, consisting of cropped, nested bifolios; front flyleaf, title page (fol. 1r), songs (fols. 1v–27v), blank pages with staves (fols. 28r–31r), blank pages (fols. 31v–32v), end flyleaf; in all 64 unnumbered pages (fols. 1r–28v have been numbered). Hand-ruled paper, 4 staves (10 mm; two-stave rastrum used) in light black ink and music in black ink; margins drawn as a red double line. The source includes 37 numbered arias for voice and keyboard by various composers and shows no signs of wear.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
